    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `contactPreference` field is now returned on the owner response, `EMAIL` when an email is present and `PHONE` otherwise. I placed each piece where it belongs, following the existing derived-field conventions (`Locality`, `MembershipLevel`):\n\n1. **`model/ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 an enum `{ EMAIL, PHONE }` with a `forOwner(Owner)` factory that holds the single rule (non-blank email \u2192 `EMAIL`, else `PHONE`). This mirrors how other derivations live as small, single-responsibility model helpers.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, styled like the neighboring derived `locality` field, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired the field via a `@Mapping` expression to a small `contactPreference(owner)` default method that delegates to `ContactPreference.forOwner(...).name()`, matching the existing `locality`/`membershipLevel` mapping style (including the null-owner guard).\n\nNo logic was copied and no class became a catch-all \u2014 the rule lives once in the model enum, and the mapper only translates.",
